      "problem": "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=11$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=15.$ Find $\\text{Var}[2X-3Y].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[2X-3Y]={(2)}^{2}\\cdot 11+{(-3)}^{2}\\cdot 15=179.\n$$",
